Source: cetrafs
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Massimo Cetra <mcetra@gmail.com>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13), dh-dkms
Standards-Version: 4.6.2
Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: cetrafs-dkms
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, dkms
Recommends: cetrafs-tools
Description: clustered shared-disk filesystem (VMFS alternative) - kernel module (DKMS)
 cetrafs is a clustered, shared-disk Linux filesystem: several nodes mount
 one shared block device (an iSCSI or FC LUN) at the same time, with VM disk
 images living directly on the one volume, the way VMFS backs vSphere. Nodes
 coordinate through the storage itself (atomic SCSI COMPARE AND WRITE), with
 no cluster network or lock manager.
 .
 This package ships the out-of-tree kernel module source and builds it with
 DKMS, so cetrafs.ko is rebuilt automatically on every kernel upgrade.

Package: cetrafs-tools
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Recommends: cetrafs-dkms
Description: clustered shared-disk filesystem (VMFS alternative) - userspace tools
 cetrafs is a clustered, shared-disk Linux filesystem (see the cetrafs-dkms
 package for the kernel module and a fuller description).
 .
 This package provides the userspace tools:
  * mkfs.cetra   - create a cetrafs volume
  * fsck.cetra   - check and repair a volume
  * defrag.cetra - online per-file defragmentation

Package: pve-storage-cetrafs
Architecture: all
Build-Profiles: <!pkg.cetrafs.nopve>
Depends: libpve-common-perl,
         libpve-storage-perl,
         ${misc:Depends},
         ${perl:Depends},
Recommends: cetrafs-dkms, cetrafs-tools
Description: clustered shared-disk filesystem (VMFS alternative) - Proxmox VE storage plugin
 cetrafs is a clustered, shared-disk Linux filesystem (see the cetrafs-dkms
 package for the kernel module and a fuller description).
 .
 This package adds the Proxmox VE storage type "cetrafs": a cetrafs volume
 on a shared LUN, mounted on every cluster node and used for VM images,
 container volumes, ISOs, templates, backups and snippets. Install it on
 every node. The web UI integration is in pve-storage-cetrafs-ui.

Package: pve-storage-cetrafs-ui
Architecture: all
Build-Profiles: <!pkg.cetrafs.nopve>
Depends: pve-manager,
         pve-storage-cetrafs (= ${binary:Version}),
         proxmox-widget-toolkit,
         ${misc:Depends},
Description: clustered shared-disk filesystem (VMFS alternative) - Proxmox VE web UI
 cetrafs is a clustered, shared-disk Linux filesystem (see the cetrafs-dkms
 package for the kernel module and a fuller description).
 .
 This optional package adds "cetrafs" to Datacenter -> Storage -> Add in
 the Proxmox VE web interface, with the dialog to add and edit a cetrafs
 storage. Without it the storage is managed with pvesm.
